# RedMart / Lazada Account Credentials
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS HERE:
# Lazada frequently expires browser sessions after some time or periods of inactivity.
# When the shopping agent opens the browser and finds that the session is signed out
# (or at an explicit login page), it can read credentials from your local `.env`
# file and automatically log in for you, avoiding the need for manual re-login each time.
#
# WHAT IT SHOULD DO:
# 1. Copy this file to `.env`:
#      cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your Lazada login email (or phone number) and password below.
# 3. When the agent navigates to Lazada / RedMart and detects an explicit login gate,
#    it will use these credentials to fill in the login form and sign in automatically
#    in the visible browser.
# 4. If Lazada triggers a CAPTCHA, slider, SMS/email OTP, passkey, or unusual-traffic challenge,
#    the agent will pause and prompt you to complete that verification step directly in
#    the visible browser.
#
# SECURITY & PRIVACY:
# - `.env` is ignored by git (.gitignore) and must NEVER be committed to version control.
# - Never share your real credentials in chat, commit messages, or public issue trackers.
# - Credentials are only used locally by the agent to fill the visible Lazada login form.

# Primary login credentials
USERNAME=your_email_or_phone@example.com
PASSWORD=your_password_here

# Optional / alternative explicit variable names (both naming styles are supported)
# LAZADA_USERNAME=your_email_or_phone@example.com
# LAZADA_PASSWORD=your_password_here
